{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-34738","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53884","text":"RFC — Evidence Residency ("},{"id":"spn-53885","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-53886","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-34739","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53887","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status."},{"id":"spn-53888","text":" Ruled (user, 2026-07-23). This RFC freezes the first non-TRVM TRAAVIIS environment "},{"id":"spn-53889","marks":["italic"],"text":"before any code is written"},{"id":"spn-53890","text":". It scopes exactly one task, one one-shot agent interface, and the snapshot / output / verifier / reward / replayability contracts. Nothing here requires WallRiderLang lowering or TRVM interaction-calculus reduction. Code is held until these contracts are frozen."}]},{"id":"blk-34740","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53891","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-53892","text":" TRAAVIIS is an "},{"id":"spn-53893","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environment for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-53894","text":". Its value is not \"deterministic worlds\" but: "},{"id":"spn-53895","marks":["italic"],"text":"an agent's work should leave inspectable evidence that survives replay, verification, disagreement, and human review."},{"id":"spn-53896","text":" Evidence Residency is the first environment that makes that concrete for a real repository, and it is deliberately "},{"id":"spn-53897","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53898","text":" a TRVM world."}]},{"id":"blk-34741","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53899","text":"1. Substrate ruling — TRAAVIIS is substrate-neutral"}]},{"id":"blk-34742","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53900","text":"TRAAVIIS evaluates over multiple substrates. TRVM is one — uniquely strong, but no longer the definition of everything TRAAVIIS can evaluate."}]},{"id":"blk-34743","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRAAVIIS\nsubstrate-neutral evaluation and evidence layer\n        │\n        ├── TRVM substrate            (trvm.world.v1)\n        │     sem · scen · film\n        │     reference · native · oracle\n        │\n        └── Residency substrate       (residency.repository.v1)\n              snapshot · finding · patch · trace\n              citations · patch · tests · identity"},{"id":"blk-34744","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53901","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-53902","text":" is an "},{"id":"spn-53903","marks":["bold"],"text":"external evidence environment orchestrated by TRAAVIIS"},{"id":"spn-53904","text":". TRAAVIIS prepares a frozen subject, runs an agent command in a controlled workspace, collects evidence, and checks it with external deterministic verifiers. It does not fold anything through "},{"id":"spn-53905","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-53906","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-53907","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-53908","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34745","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53909","text":"2. The common ladder (shared) vs substrate-specific artifacts"}]},{"id":"blk-34746","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53910","text":"Four constructs are "},{"id":"spn-53911","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-53912","text":" across every substrate:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34748","spans":[{"id":"spn-53913","text":"construct"}]},{"id":"blk-34749","spans":[{"id":"spn-53914","text":"question it answers"}]}],"id":"blk-34747","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34750","spans":[{"id":"spn-53915","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34751","spans":[{"id":"spn-53916","text":"what must be done?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34752","spans":[{"id":"spn-53917","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34753","spans":[{"id":"spn-53918","text":"how is admissible evidence scored?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34754","spans":[{"id":"spn-53919","marks":["code"],"text":"SubstrateProfileV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34755","spans":[{"id":"spn-53920","text":"how is the subject prepared and evidence collected?"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34756","spans":[{"id":"spn-53921","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34757","spans":[{"id":"spn-53922","text":"what happened, what was produced, what passed, what score?"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34758","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53923","text":"Substrate-specific evidence lives "},{"id":"spn-53924","marks":["bold"],"text":"below"},{"id":"spn-53925","text":" the shared ladder:"}]},{"id":"blk-34759","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"TRVM       sem · scen · film\nResidency  snap · trace · finding · patch"},{"id":"blk-34760","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53926","text":"2a. Correction — "},{"id":"spn-53927","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-53928","text":" is TRVM-only; the neutral trace is "},{"id":"spn-53929","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-34761","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53930","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-53931","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…` is a TRVM deterministic-execution artifact"},{"id":"spn-53932","text":" and stays that way. It does "},{"id":"spn-53933","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53934","text":" generalize to arbitrary substrates. The substrate-neutral observable record is a "},{"id":"spn-53935","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-53936","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-53937","marks":["bold"],"text":"shared"},{"id":"spn-53938","text":" object is the "},{"id":"spn-53939","marks":["bold"],"text":"`episode-…`"},{"id":"spn-53940","text":" receipt, which references whichever substrate-specific evidence exists plus a "},{"id":"spn-53941","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile"},{"id":"spn-53942","text":". We do not pretend the underlying execution mechanisms are identical."}]},{"id":"blk-34762","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53943","text":"3. Three meanings of \"replay\" (freeze this distinction)"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34764","spans":[{"id":"spn-53944","text":"level"}]},{"id":"blk-34765","spans":[{"id":"spn-53945","text":"meaning"}]},{"id":"blk-34766","spans":[{"id":"spn-53946","text":"who supports it"}]}],"id":"blk-34763","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34767","spans":[{"id":"spn-53947","marks":["bold"],"text":"exact replay"}]},{"id":"blk-34768","spans":[{"id":"spn-53948","text":"re-running canonical inputs reproduces the same state trajectory and film"}]},{"id":"blk-34769","spans":[{"id":"spn-53949","text":"TRVM"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34770","spans":[{"id":"spn-53950","marks":["bold"],"text":"action replay"}]},{"id":"blk-34771","spans":[{"id":"spn-53951","text":"recorded tool calls are reapplied against the same frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-34772","spans":[{"id":"spn-53952","text":"a controlled Residency runner, "},{"id":"spn-53953","marks":["italic"],"text":"later"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34773","spans":[{"id":"spn-53954","marks":["bold"],"text":"verification replay"}]},{"id":"blk-34774","spans":[{"id":"spn-53955","text":"the submitted finding, patch and receipts are re-checked against the frozen snapshot"}]},{"id":"blk-34775","spans":[{"id":"spn-53956","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34776","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53957","marks":["bold"],"text":"Residency v1 promises only verification replay."},{"id":"spn-53958","text":" We do "},{"id":"spn-53959","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-53960","text":" promise deterministic replay of an arbitrary external coding-agent process — shell tools, package registries, clocks, and OS behaviour make that a much larger claim. Residency v1 honestly promises:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34778","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53961","text":"The evidence and outcome can be independently reverified."}]}],"id":"blk-34777","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-34779","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53962","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1.replayability"},{"id":"spn-53963","text":" records which level applies ("},{"id":"spn-53964","marks":["code"],"text":"exact"},{"id":"spn-53965","text":" for TRVM, "},{"id":"spn-53966","marks":["code"],"text":"verification"},{"id":"spn-53967","text":" for Residency v1)."}]},{"id":"blk-34780","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-53968","text":"4. Frozen subject — "},{"id":"spn-53969","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1"},{"id":"spn-53970","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-53971","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]},{"id":"blk-34781","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53972","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-53973","text":" seals "},{"id":"spn-53974","marks":["bold"],"text":"only the subject"},{"id":"spn-53975","text":" — the repository the agent sees — "},{"id":"spn-53976","marks":["bold"],"text":"not the evaluation procedure"},{"id":"spn-53977","text":". The same frozen repository must remain the same "},{"id":"spn-53978","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-53979","text":" even when evaluated under a different test plan."}]},{"id":"blk-34782","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"snapshot_version\": \"residency.snapshot.v1\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"snap-…\",\n  \"files\": { \"<relpath>\": \"<content-hash>\", … },\n  \"exclusions\": [ \"<glob>\", … ],\n  \"file_modes\": { \"<relpath>\": \"0755\", … },\n  \"base_revision\": \"<vcs-rev or null>\",\n  \"visible_config\": { … } }"},{"id":"blk-34783","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53980","text":"Seal: repository bytes, normalized relative paths, file modes, exclusions, base revision if available, task-visible repository config. "},{"id":"spn-53981","marks":["bold"],"text":"Do not seal"},{"id":"spn-53982","text":" timestamps or absolute machine paths — they would make the snapshot machine-specific without changing its meaning. "},{"id":"spn-53983","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-53984","text":" is a content hash of the canonical sealed bytes."}]},{"id":"blk-34784","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53985","marks":["bold"],"text":"Ownership split (erratum)."},{"id":"spn-53986","text":" The evaluation procedure lives in "},{"id":"spn-53987","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-53988","text":", not the snapshot:"}]},{"id":"blk-34785","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34787","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53989","marks":["bold"],"text":"`SnapshotV1`"},{"id":"spn-53990","text":" seals — repository bytes, relative paths, file modes,"}]}],"id":"blk-34786","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34788","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53991","text":"exclusions, base revision, task-visible repository config."}]},{"id":"blk-34789","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34791","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53992","marks":["bold"],"text":"`TaskSpecV1`"},{"id":"spn-53993","text":" seals — declared test commands, required toolchain"}]}],"id":"blk-34790","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34792","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53994","text":"constraints, the verifier plan, and the agent execution policy (§7)."}]},{"id":"blk-34793","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34795","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-53995","marks":["bold"],"text":"`EpisodeReceiptV1`"},{"id":"spn-53996","text":" records — "},{"id":"spn-53997","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-53998","text":" toolchain versions, "},{"id":"spn-53999","marks":["italic"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-54000","text":" verifier"}]}],"id":"blk-34794","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34796","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54001","text":"versions, command exit codes, and platform facts relevant to verification."}]},{"id":"blk-34797","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54002","text":"This yields the right mutation behaviour:"}]},{"id":"blk-34798","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository bytes   → snap / task / episode may move\nchange test command       → task / episode move ; snap unchanged\nrun on a different actual toolchain → episode moves ; task and snap stable"},{"id":"blk-34799","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54003","text":"5. Agent outputs — "},{"id":"spn-54004","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-54005","text":", "},{"id":"spn-54006","marks":["code"],"text":"PatchV1"},{"id":"spn-54007","text":", "},{"id":"spn-54008","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"}]},{"id":"blk-34800","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"FindingV1 → finding-…    structured claims + citations (not only prose)\nPatchV1   → patch-…      a unified diff that applies to a clean snapshot copy\nTraceV1   → trace-…      substrate-neutral record of observable process events"},{"id":"blk-34801","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54009","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-54010","text":" must carry "},{"id":"spn-54011","marks":["bold"],"text":"structured"},{"id":"spn-54012","text":" claims and citations, each citation resolving to exact supporting material inside the snapshot. Spans are "},{"id":"spn-54013","marks":["bold"],"text":"1-based inclusive line ranges"},{"id":"spn-54014","text":" expressed as an explicit object (never an ambiguous two-element array), and the "},{"id":"spn-54015","marks":["code"],"text":"quote"},{"id":"spn-54016","text":" must match the normalized snapshot bytes exactly:"}]},{"id":"blk-34802","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"finding_version\": \"residency.finding.v1\",\n  \"finding_id\": \"finding-…\",\n  \"claims\": [ { \"statement\": \"…\",\n                \"citations\": [ { \"path\": \"spec/WRL_CORE_0.1.md\",\n                                 \"start_line\": 120, \"end_line\": 138,\n                                 \"quote\": \"…\" } ] } ] }"},{"id":"blk-34803","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54017","marks":["code"],"text":"TraceV1"},{"id":"spn-54018","text":" records observable events — enough to review and to drive "},{"id":"spn-54019","marks":["italic"],"text":"action replay"},{"id":"spn-54020","text":" later, without claiming determinism now."}]},{"id":"blk-34804","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54021","text":"5a. Canonical evidence rules (freeze before generating any IDs)"}]},{"id":"blk-34805","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54022","marks":["bold"],"text":"Snapshot paths."},{"id":"spn-54023","text":" UTF-8 relative POSIX paths; no absolute paths; no "},{"id":"spn-54024","marks":["code"],"text":".."},{"id":"spn-54025","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-54026","marks":["code"],"text":"/"},{"id":"spn-54027","text":" separator on every platform; explicit symlink policy (v1: symlinks excluded); explicit line-ending policy (v1: normalize to LF for text, byte-exact for declared-binary)."}]},{"id":"blk-34806","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54028","marks":["bold"],"text":"Citations."},{"id":"spn-54029","text":" 1-based inclusive line ranges as "},{"id":"spn-54030","marks":["code"],"text":"{start_line, end_line}"},{"id":"spn-54031","text":"; the quoted text matches the normalized snapshot bytes exactly."}]},{"id":"blk-34807","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54032","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patches."},{"id":"spn-54033","text":" Unified diff; relative paths only; no timestamps; fixed "},{"id":"spn-54034","marks":["code"],"text":"a/"},{"id":"spn-54035","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-54036","marks":["code"],"text":"b/"},{"id":"spn-54037","text":" prefixes; LF line endings; "},{"id":"spn-54038","marks":["bold"],"text":"no binary patches in v1"},{"id":"spn-54039","text":"; canonical file ordering (sorted by POSIX path)."}]},{"id":"blk-34808","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54040","marks":["bold"],"text":"Traces."},{"id":"spn-54041","text":" Exclude volatile timestamps and host paths from "},{"id":"spn-54042","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-54043","text":" identity. The canonical trace records deterministic events only:"}]},{"id":"blk-34809","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"command argv · relative cwd · declared environment keys · exit code\nstdout digest · stderr digest · files-created digest · files-modified digest\nresult-file digest"},{"id":"blk-34810","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54044","text":"Human-readable timed logs may exist beside the canonical trace "},{"id":"spn-54045","marks":["bold"],"text":"without"},{"id":"spn-54046","text":" entering its identity."}]},{"id":"blk-34811","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54047","text":"6. Verifier applicability — four states"}]},{"id":"blk-34812","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54048","text":"Every verifier returns exactly one of:"}]},{"id":"blk-34813","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"pass · fail · not_applicable · error"},{"id":"blk-34814","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54049","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54050","text":" "},{"id":"spn-54051","marks":["bold"],"text":"must remain distinct"},{"id":"spn-54052","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-54053","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54054","text":": an unavailable test runner is not evidence that the candidate patch is wrong. "},{"id":"spn-54055","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-54056","text":" is coverage honesty (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-54057","marks":["code"],"text":"native"},{"id":"spn-54058","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-54059","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"},{"id":"spn-54060","text":" on a Residency episode). The receipt's verification map is "},{"id":"spn-54061","marks":["bold"],"text":"total"},{"id":"spn-54062","text":" — every declared verifier reports one of the four."}]},{"id":"blk-34815","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54063","text":"Residency v1 verifier set:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34817","spans":[{"id":"spn-54064","text":"verifier"}]},{"id":"blk-34818","spans":[{"id":"spn-54065","text":"checks"}]}],"id":"blk-34816","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34819","spans":[{"id":"spn-54066","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"}]},{"id":"blk-34820","spans":[{"id":"spn-54067","text":"every finding citation resolves and the quote matches source"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34821","spans":[{"id":"spn-54068","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"}]},{"id":"blk-34822","spans":[{"id":"spn-54069","text":"the patch applies cleanly to a fresh copy of "},{"id":"spn-54070","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34823","spans":[{"id":"spn-54071","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"}]},{"id":"blk-34824","spans":[{"id":"spn-54072","text":"the declared "},{"id":"spn-54073","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-54074","text":" pass on the patched copy"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34825","spans":[{"id":"spn-54075","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"}]},{"id":"blk-34826","spans":[{"id":"spn-54076","text":"semantic identity moved only within allowed domains"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34827","spans":[{"id":"spn-54077","marks":["code"],"text":"native"}]},{"id":"blk-34828","spans":[{"id":"spn-54078","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-54079","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34829","spans":[{"id":"spn-54080","marks":["code"],"text":"oracle"}]},{"id":"blk-34830","spans":[{"id":"spn-54081","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-54082","text":" (TRVM-only)"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34831","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54083","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-54084","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-54085","text":" verifier is where TRVM's guarantees re-enter: if the task touches a WRL world, the frozen "},{"id":"spn-54086","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-54087","text":" domains that must not move are checked with the existing Forge re-lower — a Residency episode can "},{"id":"spn-54088","marks":["italic"],"text":"depend on"},{"id":"spn-54089","text":" a TRVM identity check without "},{"id":"spn-54090","marks":["italic"],"text":"being"},{"id":"spn-54091","text":" a TRVM fold."}]},{"id":"blk-34832","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54092","text":"6a. Verifier state → reward behavior (frozen)"}]},{"id":"blk-34833","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54093","text":"The four verifier states map to reward behavior by a fixed table. "},{"id":"spn-54094","marks":["bold"],"text":"A test runner failure is not evidence that the agent's work was incorrect"},{"id":"spn-54095","text":" — it is substrate unavailability, and it must never be scored as a "},{"id":"spn-54096","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54097","text":"."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-34835","spans":[{"id":"spn-54098","text":"State"}]},{"id":"blk-34836","spans":[{"id":"spn-54099","text":"Reward behavior"}]}],"id":"blk-34834","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-34837","spans":[{"id":"spn-54100","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"}]},{"id":"blk-34838","spans":[{"id":"spn-54101","text":"signal receives its positive value"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34839","spans":[{"id":"spn-54102","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"}]},{"id":"blk-34840","spans":[{"id":"spn-54103","text":"signal receives zero; applicable floors/caps run"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34841","spans":[{"id":"spn-54104","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-34842","spans":[{"id":"spn-54105","text":"allowed only when the task declares the signal non-required"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34843","spans":[{"id":"spn-54106","marks":["code"],"text":"error"}]},{"id":"blk-34844","spans":[{"id":"spn-54107","text":"episode "},{"id":"spn-54108","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-54109","text":" becomes "},{"id":"spn-54110","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54111","text":"; reward is "},{"id":"spn-54112","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-54113","text":", not "},{"id":"spn-54114","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34845","spans":[{"id":"spn-54115","text":"required verifier returns "},{"id":"spn-54116","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"}]},{"id":"blk-34846","spans":[{"id":"spn-54117","text":"invalid task configuration ("},{"id":"spn-54118","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-54119","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-34847","spans":[{"id":"spn-54120","text":"snapshot tampering"}]},{"id":"blk-34848","spans":[{"id":"spn-54121","text":"invalid episode ("},{"id":"spn-54122","marks":["code"],"text":"status: invalid"},{"id":"spn-54123","text":"); reward "},{"id":"spn-54124","marks":["code"],"text":"0"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-34849","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54125","text":"The distinction between "},{"id":"spn-54126","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-54127","text":" (an "},{"id":"spn-54128","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54129","text":" episode: scoring could not be computed) and "},{"id":"spn-54130","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-54131","text":" (a real "},{"id":"spn-54132","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54133","text":" or a tamper) is load-bearing. Downstream aggregation must drop "},{"id":"spn-54134","marks":["code"],"text":"null"},{"id":"spn-54135","text":"-reward episodes, never average them in as zeros."}]},{"id":"blk-34850","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54136","text":"7. Reward — deterministic, decomposable, no LLM prose judging"}]},{"id":"blk-34851","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54137","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-54138","text":" for the first task is a "},{"id":"spn-54139","marks":["bold"],"text":"canonical keyed signal map"},{"id":"spn-54140","text":" (see "},{"id":"spn-54141","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"},{"id":"spn-54142","text":" §2): each key binds one verifier result to one weight. The identifiers are load-bearing — renaming a signal moves "},{"id":"spn-54143","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-54144","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34852","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"citations             → residency.citations.v1   0.25\npatch                 → residency.patch.v1        0.20\ntests                 → residency.tests.v1        0.30\nidentity              → residency.identity.v1     0.15\nfinding_completeness  → residency.finding.v1      0.10"},{"id":"blk-34853","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54145","marks":["bold"],"text":"`finding completeness` means required structured fields + evidence coverage"},{"id":"spn-54146","text":", never prose quality judged by another model. No signal in Residency v1 calls an LLM; every signal is a pure function over sealed evidence."}]},{"id":"blk-34854","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54147","marks":["bold"],"text":"Hard floors (caps, applied after the weighted sum):"}]},{"id":"blk-34855","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"patch does not apply        → reward ≤ 0.25\ncitations do not resolve    → reward ≤ 0.25\nrequired tests regress      → reward ≤ 0.40\ntampered snapshot           → reward = 0 and episode marked invalid"},{"id":"blk-34856","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54148","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-54149","text":" is the content hash of the canonical "},{"id":"spn-54150","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-54151","text":" (weights + floors + verifier binding)."}]},{"id":"blk-34857","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54152","text":"8. First task (one, narrow, bounded)"}]},{"id":"blk-34858","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"task: residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001\n\nIdentify one real inconsistency between a frozen WallRiderLang specification and\nits implementation. Cite the exact conflicting evidence, propose the smallest\npatch, run the declared acceptance checks, and preserve identities that should\nnot move."},{"id":"blk-34859","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54153","text":"Bounded corpus, explicit success contract. The agent is "},{"id":"spn-54154","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-54155","text":" asked to search for any possible improvement — it is given a fixed snapshot and a single, checkable objective."}]},{"id":"blk-34860","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54156","text":"9. Mutation laws (freeze; test-first before code)"}]},{"id":"blk-34861","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"change repository input\n  → snap / task / trace / finding / patch / episode may move\n\nchange task instructions\n  → task / episode move\n  → snap unchanged\n\nchange reward weights\n  → rew / episode move\n  → snap / trace / finding / patch unchanged\n\nchange agent output\n  → finding / patch / trace / episode move\n  → task / snap unchanged\n\nrerun the SAME verifier versions over identical frozen artifacts\n  UNDER identical canonical execution facts\n  → episode identity remains stable\n\nchange verifier implementation version\n  OR change canonical execution facts (toolchain, exit codes, platform)\n  → episode moves\n  → underlying evidence artifacts (snap / trace / finding / patch) unchanged"},{"id":"blk-34862","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54157","text":"The stability law is stated precisely because the receipt records "},{"id":"spn-54158","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-54159","text":". Stability holds only when "},{"id":"spn-54160","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-54161","text":" the verifier versions "},{"id":"spn-54162","marks":["bold"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-54163","text":" the "},{"id":"spn-54164","marks":["italic"],"text":"canonical"},{"id":"spn-54165","text":" execution facts are identical; changing either moves the "},{"id":"spn-54166","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-54167","text":". (The "},{"id":"spn-54168","marks":["italic"],"text":"volatile"},{"id":"spn-54169","text":" execution facts — wall-clock, absolute paths, transient PIDs — are excluded from the hash, so they never move it.) This reconciles with the already-stated law that a different "},{"id":"spn-54170","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual"},{"id":"spn-54171","text":" toolchain moves the episode: "},{"id":"spn-54172","marks":["bold"],"text":"verifier versions and canonical execution facts are recorded in the receipt"},{"id":"spn-54173","text":", so a scoring-logic change or a toolchain change is auditable and moves the "},{"id":"spn-54174","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-54175","text":" without rewriting what the agent actually produced."}]},{"id":"blk-34863","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54176","text":"10. "},{"id":"spn-54177","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-54178","text":" — the one-shot interface (first implementation)"}]},{"id":"blk-34864","kind":"code","language":"bash","text":"trvs eval-one residency/wrl-spec-impl-inconsistency-001.json \\\n  --agent-command \"./stub-agent\""},{"id":"blk-34865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54179","text":"The agent command receives a frozen workspace and emits one structured final result:"}]},{"id":"blk-34866","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"format\": \"traaviis.agent-result.v1\",\n  \"finding\": { \"summary\": \"…\", \"citations\": [ … ] },\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-34867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54180","text":"TRAAVIIS then, independently and deterministically:"}]},{"id":"blk-34868","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34870","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54181","text":"snapshots the starting repository → "},{"id":"spn-54182","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-54183","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34869","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34872","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54184","text":"runs the command in a controlled workspace;"}]}],"id":"blk-34871","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34874","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54185","text":"captures observable process events → "},{"id":"spn-54186","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-54187","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34873","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34876","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54188","text":"reads the proposed finding and patch → "},{"id":"spn-54189","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-54190","text":", "},{"id":"spn-54191","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-54192","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34875","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34878","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54193","text":"resolves citations against "},{"id":"spn-54194","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-54195","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34877","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34880","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54196","text":"applies the patch to a clean copy of "},{"id":"spn-54197","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-54198","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34879","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34882","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54199","text":"runs the declared "},{"id":"spn-54200","marks":["code"],"text":"test_commands"},{"id":"spn-54201","text":";"}]}],"id":"blk-34881","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34884","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54202","text":"measures identity movement;"}]}],"id":"blk-34883","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54203","text":"calculates the reward (weights + floors);"}]}],"id":"blk-34885","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54204","text":"emits "},{"id":"spn-54205","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-54206","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-34887","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-34889","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54207","text":"A richer interactive N-step action protocol (and the ORS adapter over the Episode Kernel) can follow "},{"id":"spn-54208","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-54209","text":" this one-shot path works and is boring."}]},{"id":"blk-34890","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54210","text":"10a. "},{"id":"spn-54211","marks":["code"],"text":"AgentRunPolicyV1"},{"id":"spn-54212","text":" — the frozen one-shot execution policy"}]},{"id":"blk-34891","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54213","text":"The task carries an "},{"id":"spn-54214","marks":["code"],"text":"agent_run_policy"},{"id":"spn-54215","text":" sub-document. It is part of the "},{"id":"spn-54216","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-54217","text":" identity: changing how the agent is allowed to run changes "},{"id":"spn-54218","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-54219","text":". The runner enforces it; the receipt records what actually happened."}]},{"id":"blk-34892","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"policy_version\": \"traaviis.agent-run-policy.v1\",\n  \"command_mode\": \"argv\",\n  \"shell\": false,\n  \"network\": \"disabled\",\n  \"timeout_seconds\": 900,\n  \"max_output_bytes\": 4194304,\n  \"environment\": { \"LANG\": \"C.UTF-8\", \"HOME\": \"/sandbox/home\" },\n  \"toolchain_profile\": \"residency.python-3.11.v1\",\n  \"writable_paths\": [\".\"],\n  \"result_path\": \"result.json\",\n  \"patch_path\": \"candidate.patch\" }"},{"id":"blk-34893","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54220","text":"Rules:"}]},{"id":"blk-34894","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54221","marks":["bold"],"text":"`command_mode: argv`, `shell: false`"},{"id":"spn-54222","text":" — the agent command is an argv vector"}]}],"id":"blk-34895","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54223","text":"executed without a shell. No shell interpolation is part of the contract."}]},{"id":"blk-34898","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54224","marks":["bold"],"text":"`network: disabled`"},{"id":"spn-54225","text":" by default — a task that needs the network must declare"}]}],"id":"blk-34899","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34901","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54226","text":"it explicitly, and that declaration moves "},{"id":"spn-54227","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-54228","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34902","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54229","marks":["bold"],"text":"`timeout_seconds` / `max_output_bytes`"},{"id":"spn-54230","text":" are hard bounds. Exceeding either"}]}],"id":"blk-34903","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34905","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54231","text":"terminates the run; the episode records the termination reason and the affected verifier reports "},{"id":"spn-54232","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54233","text":" (substrate unavailability), not "},{"id":"spn-54234","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54235","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34906","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54236","marks":["bold"],"text":"`environment` is a sealed key→value map, not a host allowlist."},{"id":"spn-54237","text":" Host"}]}],"id":"blk-34907","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54238","text":"environment values ("},{"id":"spn-54239","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-54240","text":", "},{"id":"spn-54241","marks":["code"],"text":"HOME"},{"id":"spn-54242","text":", "},{"id":"spn-54243","marks":["code"],"text":"LANG"},{"id":"spn-54244","text":", …) are "},{"id":"spn-54245","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-54246","text":" inherited — their values could change behavior without entering "},{"id":"spn-54247","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-54248","text":", which would break the frozen-subject claim. Only the sealed keys with their "},{"id":"spn-54249","marks":["bold"],"text":"fixed, normalized values"},{"id":"spn-54250","text":" are exported; everything else is stripped. The runner constructs a controlled "},{"id":"spn-54251","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-54252","text":" from the "},{"id":"spn-54253","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-54254","text":"; it never inherits the host's arbitrary "},{"id":"spn-54255","marks":["code"],"text":"PATH"},{"id":"spn-54256","text":". An allowlist is safe only when "},{"id":"spn-54257","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-54258","text":" the key "},{"id":"spn-54259","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-54260","text":" its normalized value are fixed, which is exactly what a sealed map is."}]},{"id":"blk-34910","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54261","marks":["bold"],"text":"`toolchain_profile`"},{"id":"spn-54262","text":" names the sealed toolchain (interpreter, package set)."}]}],"id":"blk-34911","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34913","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54263","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-54264","marks":["bold"],"text":"actual resolved executables and versions"},{"id":"spn-54265","text":" go into the receipt's "},{"id":"spn-54266","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-54267","text":", so a toolchain drift is auditable and moves "},{"id":"spn-54268","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-54269","text":" (see §9), while the "},{"id":"spn-54270","marks":["italic"],"text":"declared"},{"id":"spn-54271","text":" profile is part of "},{"id":"spn-54272","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-54273","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34914","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34916","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54274","marks":["bold"],"text":"`writable_paths`"},{"id":"spn-54275","text":" scopes filesystem mutation; writes outside the set are a"}]}],"id":"blk-34915","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54276","text":"policy violation that invalidates the episode."}]},{"id":"blk-34918","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-34920","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54277","marks":["bold"],"text":"`result_path` / `patch_path`"},{"id":"spn-54278","text":" are where the runner reads the structured"}]}],"id":"blk-34919","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-34921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54279","text":"result and the candidate patch after the process exits. Absence of a required output is a "},{"id":"spn-54280","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54281","text":" for the corresponding verifier, never an "},{"id":"spn-54282","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54283","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34922","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54284","text":"The distinction is deliberate: a "},{"id":"spn-54285","marks":["bold"],"text":"policy or substrate failure"},{"id":"spn-54286","text":" (timeout, output cap, missing runner) yields "},{"id":"spn-54287","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54288","text":"; a "},{"id":"spn-54289","marks":["bold"],"text":"missing or malformed agent output"},{"id":"spn-54290","text":" yields "},{"id":"spn-54291","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-54292","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34923","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54293","text":"11. Example receipts"}]},{"id":"blk-34924","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54294","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM episode"},{"id":"spn-54295","text":" (Golden Spinner, unchanged):"}]},{"id":"blk-34925","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"film-…\",\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"pass\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"reference\": \"1\", \"native\": \"1\", \"oracle\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"exact\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"reducer\": \"ic32\", \"epochs\": 9 } }"},{"id":"blk-34926","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54296","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency episode:"}]},{"id":"blk-34927","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\",\n  \"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\",\n  \"subject\": { \"snapshot\": \"snap-…\" },\n  \"trace\": \"trace-…\",\n  \"outputs\": { \"finding\": \"finding-…\", \"patch\": \"patch-…\" },\n  \"verification\": { \"citations\": \"pass\", \"patch\": \"pass\", \"tests\": \"pass\",\n                    \"identity\": \"pass\",\n                    \"native\": \"not_applicable\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" },\n  \"verifier_versions\": { \"citations\": \"1\", \"patch\": \"1\", \"tests\": \"1\", \"identity\": \"1\" },\n  \"reward\": 1.0,\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"validity\": \"valid\",\n  \"replayability\": \"verification\",\n  \"execution_facts\": { \"exit_code\": 0, \"platform\": \"linux-x86_64\",\n                       \"timed_out\": false, \"output_truncated\": false } }"},{"id":"blk-34928","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54297","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-54298","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-54299","marks":["code"],"text":"ok | error | invalid"},{"id":"spn-54300","text":"; "},{"id":"spn-54301","marks":["code"],"text":"validity"},{"id":"spn-54302","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-54303","marks":["code"],"text":"valid | invalid"},{"id":"spn-54304","text":". An "},{"id":"spn-54305","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-54306","text":" episode carries "},{"id":"spn-54307","marks":["code"],"text":"reward: null"},{"id":"spn-54308","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-34929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54309","text":"Canonical "},{"id":"spn-54310","marks":["code"],"text":"execution_facts"},{"id":"spn-54311","text":" — including resolved toolchain versions, normalized platform, exit codes, timeout state, and output-truncation state — enter the "},{"id":"spn-54312","marks":["code"],"text":"episode_id"},{"id":"spn-54313","text":" hash. Volatile execution metadata — wall-clock timestamps, absolute paths, transient process IDs, and host-specific log locations — is excluded."}]},{"id":"blk-34930","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54314","text":"Same ladder, honest about different execution mechanisms."}]},{"id":"blk-34931","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-54315","text":"12. Held until this RFC is accepted"}]},{"id":"blk-34932","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54316","text":"Not built now: the interactive N-step environment protocol, ORS/MCP adapters, batch "},{"id":"spn-54317","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-54318","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-54319","marks":["code"],"text":"compare"},{"id":"spn-54320","text":", action replay, a second Residency task, process rewards, and any new identity category beyond "},{"id":"spn-54321","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-54322","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-54323","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-54324","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-54325","marks":["code"],"text":"finding-…"},{"id":"spn-54326","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-54327","marks":["code"],"text":"patch-…"},{"id":"spn-54328","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-54329","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-54330","text":". Spinner Bench v0.7-5 proceeds independently and is not a blocker for this RFC."}]},{"id":"blk-34933","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-54331","text":"MIT licensed · TRAAVIIS Holdings · part of the [&] Protocol ecosystem."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera5ag32stykqanxtjfoor2zsmgea4jdsn76il3k7hrbhdgdvn2kt3a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}